      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T06:33:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Global npm alias breaks other projects\n\nAfter running socket-setup.sh and restarting the shell:\n\n```\nalias npm\u003d\"socket npm\"   # every npm command on the machine goes through socket\n```\n\nExact failure scenario: Developer runs npm install in any other project that doesn\u0027t have @socketsecurity/cli installed — socket binary intercepts the call, but the other project has no socket.yml, no token set, so it either fails or produces unexpected behavior. This is a machine-wide side effect from running a setup script in one project.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "7bd9874112e075e6ddb4721186b787028397b9fb",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5876407_82fa4002",
        "filename": "socket-setup.sh",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001955
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T13:03:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can disable that by running `socket wrapper off`  and then restarting your terminal to remove it from scanning your package installation. I believe its important to have the wrapper because most of the new vulnerabilities from npm gets sucked in with `npm i` so its good to have wrapper througout",
      "parentUuid": "251215b2_f2c4a26e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "7bd9874112e075e6ddb4721186b787028397b9fb",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54f537aa_f29f1e23",
        "filename": "socket-setup.sh",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001685
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T06:25:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Pre-commit hook can silently block commits when token is missing\n\nIn the pre-commit hook if SOCKET_CLI_API_TOKEN is not set, the script only prints a warning but still runs socket ci — which will fail with an auth error and block the commit with a confusing error. The hook should exit 0 (skip the scan) when no token is available:\n\n```\nif [ -z \"$SOCKET_CLI_API_TOKEN\" ]; then\n  echo \"Warning: SOCKET_CLI_API_TOKEN not set — skipping Socket scan.\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 65
      },
